text:
We need to count the number of bags containing 2 lollipops each. With 30 lollipops originally, after eating 2, she has 28 lollipops. Grouping them in pairs, each group of 2 lollipops fills 1 bag. There are 28 lollipops; in 14 groups of 2, thus 14 complete bags. So the answer is 14.

But check: could any be left ungrouped? 28 is divisible by 2, so all can be filled.

Answer: \boxed{14}
